  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Achieving national targets towards HIV elimination as a public health issue by facilitating access to testing to key population through community work and partnerships with Civil Society Organizations - Ecuador (01-Jan-2017-31-Dec-2019)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ecuador, HIV, Corporaci&#xf3;n Kimirina (KIMI)This program has the following goals: Contribute to achieving the 90-90-90 goals,by intensifying HIV prevention and reducing access barriers to services in key populations.. The objectives of this program are: Increase the access of key populations to HIV prevention and early diagnosis..  Promote linkages with health services, early initiation of treatment and retention of key populations..  Strengthen health services, justice and access to justice, with a focus on human rights and social participation.</narrative>
  </description>
